            <div xml:id="d24">

                <pb facs="0108" n="28" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg28"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15a3/704a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-22T11:00:00-05:00">February 22, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>131. Being somewhat disturbed, we desire that your feeling about the Conference
                    be made known to us more fully. There is undoubtedly a waning of public interest
                    here. While this may be inevitable and perhaps should not bother us, there is a
                    strong feeling here that nothing is being done to keep down the levels which in
                    every category being considered by the Conference are terribly high. I regret to
                    have to bother you, but more frequent reports are needed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
